{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1307317-confusing-instruments","id":1307317,"title":"Confusing instruments","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-04-23T15:35:38-07:00","id":1307317,"title":"Confusing instruments","content":"Bodywork, Energy and Tought Forms. To me, energy is the most confusing of all instruments. It also has almost no explanation in it's entry. I'd like to know how does this instrument work. It seems that it is using one's body internal energy as instrument to cast spells. Pretty much like using chi to fuel them. Also, I might be wrong but this looks (or could look) just like bodywork instrument.<br /> <br /> Also, when some martial artist is using hand gestures to focus his will and chi to cast a spell, isn't he also using energy?? How would energy be seen visually in-game? And how would it be different from a yoga practicioner using anything chi-related??<br /> <br /> Tought forms have kinda the same thing. I read about thought forms from real life magick. In game, the mage just creates something from his mind, imbues some intention and throw it into the universe to make his intention true? In-game is the mage just stopping for a momment (concentrating/thinking/etc) and then the spell is cast??","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-23T16:55:12-07:00","id":1307337,"title":"","content":"Bodywork is direct manipulation of the target's body through either external treatments, or through rigorous physical regimens. Manipulating chi might be part of the Focus for the character, but there is a significant difference between doing daily meditations using specific body postures to control your chi flows, and calling on your internal energy by concentrating (which would be the energy focus).<br /> <br /> In some Focuses, bodywork and energy are closely relate (Akashics being the most common group). In others it will be completely different. A Progenitor might use bodywork that looks more like a finally honed exercise routine, with biofeedback monitor and similar efforts, while they would be using energy to manipulate bio-electricity to help their neurons fire faster.<br /> <br /> With thought forms, the power of the thought form is directly related to the importance of the form. A quick thing you just concentrate on for a moment is a very weak thought form that you have spent little time structuring your mind. Spending an hour contemplating the concept of the American Dream, will do you better.<br /> <br /> In general though, remember that Instruments are important, but are designed to be flexible (at least until you get to personalized and unique instruments, but those should be specified enough to avoid any confusion). It's OK if bodywork and energy have a fuzzy line between them.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-23T19:44:40-07:00","id":1307389,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1307317-confusing-instruments?p=1307337#post1307337\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bodywork is direct manipulation of the target's body through either external treatments, or through rigorous physical regimens. Manipulating chi might be part of the Focus for the character, but there is a significant difference between doing daily meditations using specific body postures to control your chi flows, and calling on your internal energy by concentrating (which would be the energy focus).</div> </div> </div> </div>Isn't that meditation instrument? <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1307317-confusing-instruments?p=1307337#post1307337\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In some Focuses, bodywork and energy are closely relate (Akashics being the most common group). In others it will be completely different. A Progenitor might use bodywork that looks more like a finally honed exercise routine, with biofeedback monitor and similar efforts, while they would be using energy to manipulate bio-electricity to help their neurons fire faster.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wouldn't that be exertions?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1307317-confusing-instruments?p=1307337#post1307337\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With thought forms, the power of the thought form is directly related to the importance of the form. A quick thing you just concentrate on for a moment is a very weak thought form that you have spent little time structuring your mind. Spending an hour contemplating the concept of the American Dream, will do you better.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, this happens with all effects and focus. The more time the mage spends with his casting, better it is. This is translated in game as more dice to roll in rituals or a diff modifier if casting time is extended. <br /> <br /> But Thought Forms are still just this? Creating, believing, and throwing at the universe? Visually it could be the mage just closing his eyes, or concentrating in something no one sees?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-23T20:38:25-07:00","id":1307397,"title":"","content":"I think you're getting too hung up on the &quot;visual&quot; of the instrument rather than the nature of why they work to help a mage channel power. Bodywork vs. meditation is bodywork manipulates the body to influence the mind, where meditation hones the mind to control the body (besides all the other things you can do with them). You might not be able to tell the difference by watching two different mages, but that's going to happen with any largely internal focused Instrument. But this is why you start with Paradigm, then a Practice, then your Instruments. Instruments are about translating belief into power with method, since you already know the belief and method, you're picking instruments that suit that. How it looks to other people isn't important.<br /> <br /> To repeat: it's OK for there to be fuzzy lines between instruments.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-24T05:37:10-07:00","id":1307444,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1307317-confusing-instruments?p=1307397#post1307397\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think you're getting too hung up on the &quot;visual&quot; of the instrument rather than the nature of why they work to help a mage channel power. Bodywork vs. meditation is bodywork manipulates the body to influence the mind, where meditation hones the mind to control the body (besides all the other things you can do with them). You might not be able to tell the difference by watching two different mages, but that's going to happen with any largely internal focused Instrument. But this is why you start with Paradigm, then a Practice, then your Instruments. Instruments are about translating belief into power with method, since you already know the belief and method, you're picking instruments that suit that. How it looks to other people isn't important.<br /> <br /> To repeat: it's OK for there to be fuzzy lines between instruments.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes the groups of instruments are just overarching classifications. They aren't the be all and end all. A lightning-infused Etherite might use their &quot;personal electromagnetic biopulse&quot; to fuel effects, and call that an Energy instrument.<br /> <br /> An important feature to keep in mind is that the player should have a rough idea of which instruments link to which effects; there has to be a logical connection within the practice. Turning on an electrical device using Energy would make sense for such an Etherite, as would manipulating Resonance or burning someone by touch. However they would be far less likely to alter someone's memory using their personal static aura...<br /> <br /> Then again they might still use Energy for such complex effects, but mix in Lab Gear; they will use micro-electric pulses to various parts of the cortex to wipe and alter memories, for example.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-24T15:32:17-07:00","id":1307602,"title":"","content":"Well, the problema with fuzzy instruments is when you have to choose them. My martial artist wants to use his body energy to increase the power of his punches, so he concentrates on his body and breathing to cast a spell. Is he using bodywork? Is he using meditation? Or energy? Maybe all of them?<br /> <br /> Which one he should get when picking his 7 instruments? If he picks all of them, which one would work with which effect? Since they are all similar they could be used in the same kinds of effects. The same questions repeats when he drops an instrument. Looks like having those 3 is like having just one, when you drop meditation you can cast any spell that you would cast using energy or bodywork or even tought forms.<br /> <br /> Also, I got meditation vs. bodywork, being one starting in the mind and the other in the body (still too similar, but..). But I still don't get energy. It's just like that? I'm concentrating and using my inner energy?<br /> <br /> \u200bEDIT: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11620_5.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11620\" data-vbnamecard=\"11620\">twig</a> Your example is not just energy instrument. You're using devices or weapons. You might declare that it is in conjunction with energy, that's ok. But the main instrument is a device. I want to know how would be just the energy instrument, alone. One could use energy with meditation, and I think it would be just like using meditation alone.<br /> <br /> Seems that energy isn't an instrument to be used alone, I don't know. But the rules don't state any of this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3153,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","user":"Lord Revan","date":". 04-24-2019, 06:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-24T16:37:55-07:00","id":1307610,"title":"","content":"It... really feels like you're over-complicating things here. It feels like you're trying to do this in a vacuum. Most of your questions are answers by what your Paradigm is, and which Practices you use; that's what separates these things in a practical fashion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-25T00:57:23-07:00","id":1307707,"title":"","content":"Mainly it\u2019s a matter of Practice, as that\u2019s what tells you how you use your Instruments. Paradigm matters too, albeit a step removed: it\u2019s more about the Why (as in why do you think your Focus works) and the What (as in, what do you think Magick is) rather than the how. There\u2019s a reason why MRev referred to them as Theory and Practice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-25T05:45:39-07:00","id":1307730,"title":"","content":"Indeed. Parading, Practice and Instrument are separated only as a didactic tool to better explain and model the Focus. But in truth none of this existsin a vacuum, what would allow a Player (and ultimately the ST) to determine if it's correct to say you're applying meditation or energy would be the Practice first and the Paradigm second. You need the whole of the Focus to see how these things break down, and only then you can say if these overlap or not.<br /> <br /> With that in mind, it may be a pertinet question to ask the player what uses do each Instrument have. For instance, if an Akashick wants to have Martial Arts as Instrument, and also Energy (channeled trough Martial Arts), one could argue these overlap. The player would then need to explain what kind of magick uses Energy and what kind of magick uses MA alone, in order to justify taking them as different Instruments.<br /> <br /> This is entirely doable...Maybe the MA discipline the body to do stuff beyond it's normal capacity (loads of Life and Mind), and moving Energy arround (most of Prime) it's an extension of that Practice that's very related, but not always needed to do magick(tm). But if all that MA can do it's imagined by the player as Chi or viceversa, then there IS an overlap.<br /> <br /> If there is a low level of overlap, for instance Energy channeling being done trough MA alone, I would suggest not allowing to drop Energy before droping MA (otherwise you would need to ask the player to either do MA anyway to channel Energy or discover another way to channel it. Otherwise he can channel Energy doing nothing as well as ever...and would be droping two Instruments at the price of one). Remember that the order of the droping it's decided by the ST.<br /> <br /> And about Energy being always a part of an Instrument...It's true that Energy it's the perfect Instrument to combine with prety much any other instrument. However, note that while the player needs to explain how he channels energy, if Energy alone it's what's important then ANY way of channeling that energy would count. The ST needs some way to determine when you're &quot;energized&quot;, but ultimately it's the &quot;energy use&quot; rather than the physical action what counts.<br /> <br /> Most of this it's entirely narrative/interpretative, and thus it requires to have a certain level of trust on the player. If the player it's roleplaying, he or she ain't going to use Meditation when Energy was what most strongly resonates with the Effect. If the player it's going to try and game every part of the system, then Mage it's going to break. This game it's not known for it's resistance to powergaming, and this section in particular just isn't built to restrict the player.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 04-25-2019, 08:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-25T09:58:35-07:00","id":1307787,"title":"","content":"Martial art is a practice not an Instrument. Maybe you meant meditation?<br /> <br /> Are you saying that energy cannot be used alone? All instruments can be used alone with no need for other instruments or items besides themselves. <br /> <br /> I already gave an example of paradigm: a martial artist, so it could be paradigm &quot;everything is an illusion&quot;, practice: martisl art, instruments: energy, bodywork, meditation. The three kinda overlap","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-25T10:06:58-07:00","id":1307790,"title":"","content":"To give a more concrete example, one of my mages uses a lot of art in his magic, but only has one instance of &quot;Artwork&quot; as an instrument. He uses Craftwork as his main Practice, coupled with a bit of Faith, because Creation is Innately Divine and Alive, and his art is devotional to his gods.<br /> <br /> So:<br /> <br /> Artwork - this is something of a foundational Instrument (though not his personal one) that is probably going to end up dropped close to last, but primarily used when his faith doesn't dictate a specific aspect to his effort, and he's free to personally interpret his work as an act of intimate creativity. (Linked to the Art ability)<br /> <br /> Blood - His gods ain't the nicest around... and sometimes they need sacrifices. This is essential for anything that involves spending/imbuing/etc. quintessence, for him.<br /> <br /> Elements - Extremely important for impacting patterns, he invokes the gods that govern those patterns - or the changes he's going to make to them - in his art. If a particular plant happens to be sacred to a specific goddess, it would be worked directly into the art of his magic. (Linked to Craft)<br /> <br /> Language - Prayers are, of course, an element of faith, and a sacred language to use in his art, and is a way to bridge divides between both different mundane things by call on their hidden divinity, and bridging the divide between the realms of the gods and the mundane. (Linked to Expression)<br /> <br /> Music - A flip side to Elements, if he wants to call on the ephemeral associations of the gods, he plies them with music. It doesn't require specific words unless appropriately combining Language, which is generally going to mean he's doing something big. (Linked to Art or Esoterica)<br /> <br /> Ordeals - Tthere's blood, but blood can come from other things, while personal sacrifice through endurance goes a step farther to both connect with hidden mystic knowledge and the flows of time, as well as being essential - if a bit baked in - to any larger ritual.<br /> <br /> Symbols - Of course, somewhat undeniably, all of his magic comes down to using art as a symbolic representation. But specific direct symbols have specific direct meanings that aren't as fluid and experiential as art in general. If Artwork is him at his most creative with his magic, symbols are him at his most traditions, as a symbol or array of them must be precisely crafted and arranged to achieve a single result. Using divine symbols especially means going past art-as-supplication and into grabbing the living breathing blood of the world and channeling/changing it to his needs, as his personal Instruments within the larger common ones. (Linked to Occult or Esoterica)<br /> <br /> Now, are there other options I probably could have used for some of them? Yes. Language instead of Prayer is close, but I opted for language because he creates as he uses Language, not simple recites a remembered prayer and the artistic act is empowered by his mastery over words; the gods listen because of how good he is, not because of how nicely he asks.<br /> <br /> But in general, I'm hoping this example demonstrates how Practice and Paradigm make each of these Instruments come alive, and it should be pretty easy to figure out which one he'd use for most effects. Even if, externally, it might be hard to tell the difference on which Instrument is the one at the center of what he's doing (since he tends to combine them a lot anyway).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-25T10:12:14-07:00","id":1307792,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1307317-confusing-instruments?p=1307787#post1307787\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are you saying that energy cannot be used alone? All instruments can be used alone with no need for other instruments or items besides themselves.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not in the sense of &quot;as the only Instrument&quot; but in the sense of, &quot;you can't just say Energy! and have counted as using it as an Instrument.&quot; You need to explain how energy is being used in the context of Practice and Paradigm.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I already gave an example of paradigm: a martial artist, so it could be paradigm &quot;everything is an illusion&quot;, practice: martisl art, instruments: energy, bodywork, meditation. The three kinda overlap </div> </div> </div>But these are the just the shorthand words to help organize the process. Look at the example I just posted. You need to get from this stuff, to there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-25T14:05:12-07:00","id":1307840,"title":"","content":"I see. Can you give me an example where a martial artist that focuses on body energy (kudalini, chi, etc.) uses Energy instrument alone, without meditation,bodywork, gestures or any other instrument?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-25T18:20:19-07:00","id":1307908,"title":"","content":"Are you asking me to come up with the same thing I did for my character above?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-25T20:05:13-07:00","id":1307928,"title":"","content":"Don't have to be so detailed. Some of the instruments you posted similar, but they do not overlap each other and do work if used alone. I understood meditation vs. bodywork, and thought forms (even that they will look the same for someone watching the mage from outside). My issue is with energy being used as an instrument alone. <br /> <br /> I'd like an example, as detailed as you are wiling to be, of energy being used alone by some mage that has martial arts as practice. And to compare, the same from a technocrat using weird science as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-25T20:37:43-07:00","id":1307930,"title":"","content":"I think the problem is... you have to be that detailed to give an illustrative example. <br /> <br /> &quot;Martial Artist&quot; isn't enough. Can you meet me (or us if other people join in) half way and do at least the first part of my example? Start with a Paradigm and Practice (or Practices, remember you can have multiple) and how they relate. If the World is an Illusion, what is the the mage doing with their Practice about that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-25T21:40:40-07:00","id":1307941,"title":"","content":"Well, it can be as simple as that. Let's say the mage's aradigm is &quot;Everything is Chaos&quot;, he knows that there is no right Truth and that reality is shaped by belief itself. He happens to be an martial art intusiast and find it easier to use his own body energy, movements,etc. to cast his effects. His practice is only Martia Art. His instruments, among others, include energy, meditation and bodywork.<br /> <br /> So, the relation of his paradigm and practice is that he knows that his magick comes from within and his Will is what gives shape to the chaos that reality is. The best way he find to do this is through martial arts.<br /> <br /> The other example is a technocrat with &quot;A Mechanistic Cosmos&quot; paradigm that believes that reality works like a machine. If you get the right parameters you could get the result you want. His practice is Yoga and Craftwork. With them, he can build devices and tinker the gears of reality into changing what he wants. His instruments include devices,weapons,energy and symbols.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-25T22:59:36-07:00","id":1307971,"title":"","content":"Following the example of Alexander, our Martial Artist practices pankration to hone his body so he might impose his will on the world, using physical might and a strict lifestyle to tame the chaos within and without. He meditates on the Greek philosopher's words to guide his actions, and uses baths to readjust the elemental energies within. Knowing his true self, he knows that when his actions are in line with his Nature, it generates Will that does not rely on the rigors of his training to put to use.<br /> <br /> So, energy in this sense is closely tied to Willpower, but rather than &quot;spend Willpower&quot; it ties into how Nature and Willpower interact to - as put earlier - denote when he is energized and can use magic with that energy alone.<br /> <br /> --------------<br /> <br /> The technocrat example is a bit skimpy on how it's all supposed to fit together. The Yoga part especially is throwing me off compared to something more technological.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-26T11:03:18-07:00","id":1308069,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1307317-confusing-instruments?p=1307971#post1307971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, energy in this sense is closely tied to Willpower, but rather than &amp;quot;spend Willpower&amp;quot; it ties into how Nature and Willpower interact to - as put earlier - denote when he is energized and can use magic with that energy alone.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't get this part. How is he using energy? Is just willing somethinf to happen? <br /> <br /> I took a look on M20 and none of the technological/scientific practices have energy listed. So, while someone could have a technological view of yoga, the use of energy would be pretty much the same for a Technocrat. Even that je might see it from another perspective.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-26T14:05:43-07:00","id":1308116,"title":"","content":"The \u201cEnergy\u201d Instrument is specifically about life force, a concept that the Technocracy has rejected. If you want a technological/scientific Practice that deals with Energy, you should check in with the Society of Ether, and bottoms touch as Elan Vital or Orgone Energy. Dr. Frankenstein's famous achievement involved channeling life force into a corpse to reanimate it. <br /> <br /> I don't think that every Instrument can be used on its own; some, such as Blood or Energy, get used in conjunction with other Instruments. But <i>which</i> other Instruments they get used with, and how they are used, varies from Practice to Practice. In particular, Frankenstein's reanimation of a corpse featured a lot of machinery that collected Energy from the storm, processed it into a form that could animate a body, and channeled it into the body. This is different from the kinda of Instruments that Energy is usually coupled with; but it's still Energy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-26T15:32:17-07:00","id":1308144,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1307317-confusing-instruments?p=1308116#post1308116\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The \u201cEnergy\u201d Instrument is specifically about life force, a concept that the Technocracy has rejected. If you want a technological/scientific Practice that deals with Energy, you should check in with the Society of Ether, and bottoms touch as Elan Vital or Orgone Energy. Dr. Frankenstein's famous achievement involved channeling life force into a corpse to reanimate it. <br /> <br /> I don't think that every Instrument can be used on its own; some, such as Blood or Energy, get used in conjunction with other Instruments. But <i>which</i> other Instruments they get used with, and how they are used, varies from Practice to Practice. In particular, Frankenstein's reanimation of a corpse featured a lot of machinery that collected Energy from the storm, processed it into a form that could animate a body, and channeled it into the body. This is different from the kinda of Instruments that Energy is usually coupled with; but it's still Energy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, for some paradigms, energy can only be used in conjunction with another instrument. But, as you said, energy as described means life force, and this one can be used alone, or at least should. I'm trying to think how.<br /> <br /> As for blood, it can be used alone. A mage can cut his arm and use his blood directly, or if you think that cutting or the knife is another instrument, one can bite his own tongue and spit blood, or use blood from nose bleed or evem menstruation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-26T16:03:39-07:00","id":1308158,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1307317-confusing-instruments?p=1308069#post1308069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I didn't get this part. How is he using energy? Is just willing somethinf to happen?</div> </div> </div> </div>He's using energy by harnessing the energy generated in his soul while he's acting true to his nature to impose his will on the chaos of the world. For normal people this just replenished willpower, but for his Focus, it create mystical energy to power his magic.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I took a look on M20 and none of the technological/scientific practices have energy listed. </div> </div> </div>I'd assume this is because &quot;energy&quot; in the sense of an Instrument isn't really how those practices work. A plasma cannon uses energy, but those Practices are more focused on the functioning of the mechanism (so devices and weapons are the Instrument in this case) than the power behind them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So, while someone could have a technological view of yoga, the use of energy would be pretty much the same for a Technocrat. </div> </div> </div>The Yoga Practice actually spends some time on Technocratic Yoga, and they reject the mystic side of it (and the energy friendly aspects of it) for the practical side of it. A Technocratic doctor can use acupuncture - since there's a scientific explanation for why it works - for some effects, but they're not going to be manipulating the flow of<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1307317-confusing-instruments?p=1308116#post1308116\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think that every Instrument can be used on its own; some, such as Blood or Energy, get used in conjunction with other Instruments.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with most of this, but I don't think this is universally true.<br /> <br /> My mage from above has used blood alone just fine. As I noted, it's important for him if he wants to manipulate quintessence, so a lot of Prime effects can just use blood for him. I mean, he literally just anoints something with his blood if he wants to consecrate it.<br /> <br /> I'd like to think my energy example above works too.<br /> <br /> Now, for a lot of mages it might not be the case that they use certain Instruments alone (at least until they drop some), but not every one of them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-26T16:15:16-07:00","id":1308161,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> so in your example he jusy wills and, since his body is energized by his beliefs and life routine, and the effect is cast?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-26T16:45:28-07:00","id":1308172,"title":"","content":"In my example, the action the magic causes has to be affirming of his nature to use the energy; it wouldn't 'store up' over time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-26T17:30:38-07:00","id":1308177,"title":"","content":"Also, if I'm reading it correctly, it requires the expenditure of a point of Willpower above and beyond the normal requirements.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-26T18:48:32-07:00","id":1308207,"title":"","content":"I was actually avoiding that specific requirement simply because it confuses the issue. I didn't want a strict mechanical binary on when energy would apply like spending WP. The goal was to show how Focus comes together with when &quot;energy&quot; counts for this character without it being &quot;always&quot; as guided by their reliance on imposing their will on a chaotic universe requiring enacting their will in a more narrative way (hence Nature is more the key element).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-27T08:09:56-07:00","id":1308310,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1307317-confusing-instruments?p=1308172#post1308172\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In my example, the action the magic causes has to be affirming of his nature to use the energy; it wouldn't 'store up' over time.</div> </div> </div> </div>But what would be the action to cast the effect? I still dont get this.<br /> And spending Willpower point makes no sense at all rulewise. Energy would be the worst instrument ever","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-27T10:17:24-07:00","id":1308321,"title":"","content":"There wouldn't be a specific &quot;action&quot; beyond the affirmation raising their energy in a mystic nature. This would be more like the Celestial Alignment Instrument where situation, not action, is the tool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-28T13:10:27-07:00","id":1308513,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1307317-confusing-instruments?p=1308321#post1308321\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There wouldn't be a specific &quot;action&quot; beyond the affirmation raising their energy in a mystic nature. This would be more like the Celestial Alignment Instrument where situation, not action, is the tool.</div> </div> </div> </div> But the mage still has to do something. Even &quot;increasing his energy&quot; is an action. So, visually the mage can stay still and cast an effect, even that internally he is working his body energy?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-28T14:04:12-07:00","id":1308523,"title":"","content":"Is... staying still and letting the effect happen affirming the character's Nature? I highly doubt it with this concept. Someone with such a passive Nature is unlikely to have such a forceful Focus. They're imposing their will through affirming of their truest self on a wild and chaotic universe... sitting there doing nothing doesn't sound like that. But they're not inherently bound to a specific action like meditating, or taking a marital stance, or whatever, they're just bound to affirm their Nature in the situation at hand. As the book says, this is were role-playing comes in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-30T08:07:02-07:00","id":1308926,"title":"","content":"Note the capital N in \u201cNature\u201d: Heavy Arms is referring to Archetypes that all mages have, as in \u201cNature and Demeanor\u201d. If your Nature is \u201cArchitect\u201d, then affirming your Nature involves creating something. And so on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-30T09:21:24-07:00","id":1308939,"title":"","content":"Interesting. Visually, your take on the instrument is like what I thought, but internally I tought it was related more on the energy produced by the body than the mage personality. Is any of this in any book?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-30T10:46:20-07:00","id":1308968,"title":"","content":"It's not in a Mage book precisely? I'm playing off some of the early Greek philosophers as they addressed the mind/body duality issue without an understanding of biochemistry. While they didn't create a new &quot;energy&quot; like chi to explain it, they recognized that the mind seemed capable of generating excess energy in the body. Not being able to observe how adrenaline works, they could see how mood seemed to boost the energy in the body. They could see a passionate man could work on a task for days and nights on end, even skipping on food and sleep, as if the mind itself was fueling the body thanks to that passion.<br /> <br /> Then I cranked that up a bit to work for Mage.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-30T18:13:49-07:00","id":1309063,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1307317-confusing-instruments?p=1308968#post1308968\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not in a Mage book precisely? I'm playing off some of the early Greek philosophers as they addressed the mind/body duality issue without an understanding of biochemistry. While they didn't create a new &amp;quot;energy&amp;quot; like chi to explain it, they recognized that the mind seemed capable of generating excess energy in the body. Not being able to observe how adrenaline works, they could see how mood seemed to boost the energy in the body. They could see a passionate man could work on a task for days and nights on end, even skipping on food and sleep, as if the mind itself was fueling the body thanks to that passion.<br /> <br /> Then I cranked that up a bit to work for Mage.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see. That is an interesting approach. Too much mind involved if you ask me, but still cool.<br /> <br /> Can you provide an example inbplau of an effect using solely energy thay you made and how it worked out?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-30T19:34:23-07:00","id":1309077,"title":"","content":"None of my in-play mages since M20 came out use energy as an instrument (and previous editions worked a bit differently with this stuff) so I don't really have an example that I'm not making up for the thread.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-03T17:29:58-07:00","id":1309810,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Since the instruments are so fuzzy I prefer to add rules to them to keep them easy to role play, to do so I usually write small paragraphs about each one and the possible abilities they may key of when using mundane skills to improve magic.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">I'll write a bit about my Akashik Sister, Jade, and her paradigm, practices and instrument as an example.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Her paradigm is bring </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Back the Golden Age</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, once heroes and powers roamed the earth, but no more, but all hope is not lost since through hard work, careful brews and strife one can can purify and refine oneself to reach heights to match those ancient powers.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Her practice is Martial Arts to channel the hard work and find strife and Witchcraft to brew and refine potions and make crafts to help her body.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Her instruments are:</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Meditation, she uses it for large workings and rituals, is versatile with every sphere. this keys off meditation. Not useful to fast casting</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Martial Arts as a way to prove herself through strife that she is an equal to the legends gone by, this helps with forces entropy life and prime spheres.keys off with brawling, melee, martial arts or do.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Bodywork is another instrument, coming from the need to perfect her body, With her control she makes her body/pattern asume certain forms. useful using life, mind and prime spheres. keys of esoterica (body control), athletics or acrobatics.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Energy is her use of the mystical ki that flows in her body and that of others through careful control of her body and of that of other, useful in forces, prime, mind and spirit. keys of athletics, acrobatics, do and body control.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Brews is the skill to find assistance in her journey in the natural world. making concoction, potions, brews and salves she can enjoy heightened states of mind or purified body to search for improvement. Helps with life, mind, prime and spirit. Keys off Academics (botanics) esoterica (herbology) and survival. not useful to fast casting</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Bones and remains, a more gruesome instrument allows jade to commune with things dead and decaying, to siphon off her own weakness or to affects the impure world outside herself using small crafts made of bones, flesh and fur, helps with correspondence, entropy, spirit and matter, keys off crafts. can also be used in potions. not useful to fast casting.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">And lastly her last instruments are weapons, contemplate weapons and use them in battle is useful to focus herself into turning into one. useful with forces, matter and prime.keys of melee and do</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">You see, her paradigm, practice and instruments now can speak about her nature as a spellcaster. she is a magical gym sis drinking her ketamine and kicking ass, but also speak of her falencies, she sucks with connections magic, her paradigm is a personal one, and matter requires long work with crafts and meditations.</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25302-gearbox","name":"Gearbox","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-03T22:01:48-07:00","id":1309864,"title":"","content":"Hi! Welcome <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> And, nice first post.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-22T08:21:36-07:00","id":1326708,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gearbox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1307317-confusing-instruments?p=1309810#post1309810\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Since the instruments are so fuzzy I prefer to add rules to them to keep them easy to role play, to do so I usually write small paragraphs about each one and the possible abilities they may key of when using mundane skills to improve magic.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">I'll write a bit about my Akashik Sister, Jade, and her paradigm, practices and instrument as an example.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Her paradigm is bring </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Back the Golden Age</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, once heroes and powers roamed the earth, but no more, but all hope is not lost since through hard work, careful brews and strife one can can purify and refine oneself to reach heights to match those ancient powers.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Her practice is Martial Arts to channel the hard work and find strife and Witchcraft to brew and refine potions and make crafts to help her body.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Her instruments are:</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Meditation, she uses it for large workings and rituals, is versatile with every sphere. this keys off meditation. Not useful to fast casting</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Martial Arts as a way to prove herself through strife that she is an equal to the legends gone by, this helps with forces entropy life and prime spheres.keys off with brawling, melee, martial arts or do.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Bodywork is another instrument, coming from the need to perfect her body, With her control she makes her body/pattern asume certain forms. useful using life, mind and prime spheres. keys of esoterica (body control), athletics or acrobatics.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Energy is her use of the mystical ki that flows in her body and that of others through careful control of her body and of that of other, useful in forces, prime, mind and spirit. keys of athletics, acrobatics, do and body control.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Brews is the skill to find assistance in her journey in the natural world. making concoction, potions, brews and salves she can enjoy heightened states of mind or purified body to search for improvement. Helps with life, mind, prime and spirit. Keys off Academics (botanics) esoterica (herbology) and survival. not useful to fast casting</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Bones and remains, a more gruesome instrument allows jade to commune with things dead and decaying, to siphon off her own weakness or to affects the impure world outside herself using small crafts made of bones, flesh and fur, helps with correspondence, entropy, spirit and matter, keys off crafts. can also be used in potions. not useful to fast casting.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">And lastly her last instruments are weapons, contemplate weapons and use them in battle is useful to focus herself into turning into one. useful with forces, matter and prime.keys of melee and do</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">You see, her paradigm, practice and instruments now can speak about her nature as a spellcaster. she is a magical gym sis drinking her ketamine and kicking ass, but also speak of her falencies, she sucks with connections magic, her paradigm is a personal one, and matter requires long work with crafts and meditations.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>This is the kind of example I was talking about. And now I ask you this. When Jade wants to cast a Forces effect using only energy instrum, what does she do? How athletics, do or body control would work with this?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-26T06:45:48-07:00","id":1327568,"title":"","content":"Well, I have some ideas.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>M20, Energy</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The life force forms a significant element of mystic focus. Through practices like Tantra, yoga, and other forms of energy work, a person can perceive and manipulate that life force, directing it to his needs. That energy, in turn, fuels martial arts, sexual disciplines, bodywork, and other practices.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that from this text it clearly shows this Instrument it's <i>nearly </i>always going to be coupled with an activity that could be interpreted as another Instrument (among other things, it mentions bodywork as a practice, but you know it's an Instrument)...<br /> <br /> ...but that's not the same as <i>being </i>the other. I think it's more akin to having a <a href=\"https://www.swordsofmight.com/wp-content/uploads/2017/02/sd12150-1.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">sword cane</a> that can double as a sword or a wand/rod depending if you unsheathe the sword or not<br /> <br /> For instance:<br /> <br /> I could have an Akashick that has &quot;Chi&quot; as one of his Instruments, and he meditates to gather this chi. You may think that's the use of Meditation...but the thing it's that I'm not meditating to release an Effect, I'm meditating to concentrate this chi.<br /> <br /> Now I have &quot;Energy&quot; to cast an Effect afterwars. Then, when I enter combat, instead of trying to enter in a meditative state (which may be complicated) I limit myself to release that Energy.<br /> <br /> This does require to bargain with the ST how many effects can I cast (or for how long) until my chi it's expended. How many &quot;charges&quot; of Energy can my body store until I need to recharge, or how will this work. It's an Instrument, you need to have it in order to use it, but because it's so ephemeral one may need to specify <i>when </i>you're energized and not energized<br /> <br /> This &quot;coupling&quot; isn't exclusive of Energy. To use True Names you require to use Language, and spoken uses of Language require a Voice to speak. However you don't need to write all the three. You could have TN as Instrument and believe Language isn't the source of the power (and not have it as Instrument). <hr /><br /> Trying very hard to find examples that don't involve other activities that could be Instrument, this it's the &quot;purest&quot; I can think off:<br /> <br /> An Etherite that exposes himself to some kind of energy for some Mad Science reason.<br /> <br /> Like those crazy hippies that don't eat and expose themselves to sunlight all day believing that they will do photosynthesis if they try hard enough (altrough the whole experience it's probably an Ordeal).<br /> <br /> A wizard that's Focused while being bathed in sunlight sounds plausible. One may think that's requiring &quot;Celestial Alignaments&quot; (with the Sun), but because this is Energy you don't really need it to be <i>day</i>, you could summon sunlight from the other side of the planet with Correspondence (using another Instrument) to get Focused.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 07-26-2019, 09:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-26T14:02:56-07:00","id":1327648,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1307317-confusing-instruments?p=1327568#post1327568\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, I have some ideas.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I think that from this text it clearly shows this Instrument it's <i>nearly </i>always going to be coupled with an activity that could be interpreted as another Instrument (among other things, it mentions bodywork as a practice, but you know it's an Instrument)...<br /> <br /> ...but that's not the same as <i>being </i>the other. I think it's more akin to having a <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.swordsofmight.com/wp-content/uploads/2017/02/sd12150-1.jpg&amp;quot;]sword</a> cane[/URL] that can double as a sword or a wand/rod depending if you unsheathe the sword or not<br /> <br /> For instance:<br /> <br /> I could have an Akashick that has &amp;quot;Chi&amp;quot; as one of his Instruments, and he meditates to gather this chi. You may think that's the use of Meditation...but the thing it's that I'm not meditating to release an Effect, I'm meditating to concentrate this chi.<br /> <br /> Now I have &amp;quot;Energy&amp;quot; to cast an Effect afterwars. Then, when I enter combat, instead of trying to enter in a meditative state (which may be complicated) I limit myself to release that Energy.<br /> <br /> This does require to bargain with the ST how many effects can I cast (or for how long) until my chi it's expended. How many &amp;quot;charges&amp;quot; of Energy can my body store until I need to recharge, or how will this work. It's an Instrument, you need to have it in order to use it, but because it's so ephemeral one may need to specify <i>when </i>you're energized and not energized<br /> <br /> This &amp;quot;coupling&amp;quot; isn't exclusive of Energy. To use True Names you require to use Language, and spoken uses of Language require a Voice to speak. However you don't need to write all the three. You could have TN as Instrument and believe Language isn't the source of the power (and not have it as Instrument). <hr /></div> </div> </div> </div>This is a very interesting view of the instrument.<br /> Maybe, trying to separate it from any other instrument, it can be used just by wanting to raise your body energy? Much like dragonball. It could require an esoterica roll, idk.<br /> <br /> I haven't stop to think about your other examples before. Indeed there are instruments that depends on others. But with true name you still have to discover the names, whichbis one thing more to do besides speaking (language), they are not quite identical, this seems to not be the case with energy/meditation.<br /> If that is the case, having meditation and energy is like having one less instrument. All effects that can be made by energy can be made by meditation alone.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1307317-confusing-instruments?p=1327568#post1327568\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Trying very hard to find examples that don't involve other activities that could be Instrument, this it's the &amp;quot;purest&amp;quot; I can think off:<br /> <br /> An Etherite that exposes himself to some kind of energy for some Mad Science reason.<br /> <br /> Like those crazy hippies that don't eat and expose themselves to sunlight all day believing that they will do photosynthesis if they try hard enough (altrough the whole experience it's probably an Ordeal).<br /> <br /> A wizard that's Focused while being bathed in sunlight sounds plausible. One may think that's requiring &amp;quot;Celestial Alignaments&amp;quot; (with the Sun), but because this is Energy you don't really need it to be <i>day</i>, you could summon sunlight from the other side of the planet with Correspondence (using another Instrument) to get Focused.</div> </div> </div> </div>When I think of Chi, I see a constant life force, much like in dragonball Z. M20 describes energy as life energy, as coming from the body. So, while you might need to do something to tap it, it doesn't seems to come from an external source.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-29T06:28:30-07:00","id":1328077,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Maybe, trying to separate it from any other instrument, it can be used just by wanting to raise your body energy? Much like dragonball. </div> </div> </div>Dragon Ball Z characters <b>scream very loud</b> to increase their power. Kiai shouts like those can be an Instrument by themselves.<br /> <br /> They also meditate sometimes, and show their bodywork when they throw their heavy training clothes or do hand gestures when using a technique. I'm not sure if there's an example of them just raising their power w/o doing anything else. I'm sure it's not very common","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 07-29-2019, 10:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-29T17:15:31-07:00","id":1328188,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1307317-confusing-instruments?p=1328077#post1328077\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Dragon Ball Z characters <b>scream very loud</b> to increase their power. Kiai shouts like those can be an Instrument by themselves.<br /> <br /> They also meditate sometimes, and show their bodywork when they throw their heavy training clothes or do hand gestures when using a technique. I'm not sure if there's an example of them just raising their power w/o doing anything else. I'm sure it's not very common</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> They scream/gesture when going super sayajin. All the Z fighters on Earth could change their power level at will. I remember Vegeta got impressed by how they could hide and rise their powerlevel easily. <br /> But, just raising their powerlevel doesn`t mean anything. They do not cast any &quot;effect&quot; just by doing this, it like a requisite to do more powerfull deeds. I guess you are right about Energy not being able to be used alone. It would be weird for the mage to just wish to tap into his life force and just, again, wish for his effect to fire. Guess we will have to couple it with meditation or any other instrument.<br /> <br /> Also, reading Book of Shadows, the examples it gives about energy in &quot;Examples in play&quot; are kinda lame, they don't go further to explain the use of the instrument. Iirc, we have 3 examples where one is using energy together with cannibalism, the second together with bodywork and herb-lore for medicine and the last one just says that she uses Prime by skillful use of chi...<br /> <br /> What does this last one means, I don`t know.<br /> <br /> About another topic, the instrument Formulae, Equations and Math, is it just for foreseing things? How can calculating something change reality? The examples I saw was together with reality hacking (computer), is it another instrument that is dependent of others???","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-30T00:15:33-07:00","id":1328233,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1307317-confusing-instruments?p=1328188#post1328188\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How can calculating something change reality? The examples I saw was together with reality hacking (computer), is it another instrument that is dependent of others???</div> </div> </div> </div>Take the logic of mathematical foresight and just bring it to the present tense. Having proven that something will happen <i>now</i>, it does. Often coincidental. Works well for Entropy magic (probabilities) but many Traditions and Conventions might have equivalence. Syndicate quants, Turing-inspired Virtual Adepts, and Hermetic geometers come to mind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-30T22:17:30-07:00","id":1328457,"title":"","content":"Isn't calculating something = Magick a big part of Sacred Geometry as well? Atleast the smaller things. I put a fancy design on something, now it does X.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25315-jihelu","name":"Jihelu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-31T13:59:03-07:00","id":1328607,"title":"","content":"I think just calculating something to bring it to happen quite nonsense. Unless it is a divination, then it is not the calculation per se that is causing the action.<br /> So, the hermetic wants to telekinetically lift his books to his bookcase. He finds the right ammount of energy, taking in consideration all the variables including his own Will and life energy and the books just float?<br /> Or the mage wants to juice up his strength, uses formulas to determine chemistry/biology parameters and then what?<br /> I think I don't grasp how this instrument works for nore complex effects.<br /> Also, I believe it is more to be used in rituals, since it takes time to calculate. Unless the mage is a math wizard.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-31T15:03:04-07:00","id":1328618,"title":"","content":"It also kinda depends on your paradigm, calculating something to make stuff happen would be quite nonsense to a Technocracy member but maybe not to a Virtual Adept who does 'insert weird reality hacking terms here' or a Order of Hermes Mage who more or less just does calculations because of the weird resonance that math has and understands that at the end of the day it's just your will.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25315-jihelu","name":"Jihelu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-31T17:21:56-07:00","id":1328649,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jihelu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1307317-confusing-instruments?p=1328618#post1328618\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It also kinda depends on your paradigm, calculating something to make stuff happen would be quite nonsense to a Technocracy member but maybe not to a Virtual Adept who does 'insert weird reality hacking terms here' or a Order of Hermes Mage who more or less just does calculations because of the weird resonance that math has and understands that at the end of the day it's just your will.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Interesting.. Indeed, the hermetic could use equations and calculation to help him focus his will on the effect he desires. The more information he has about the effect (like, required energy, initial parameters, etc.) the better he can focus his Will into the spell. Actually, the spell IS the act of calculation.<br /> <br /> In my example, after calculating the force, acceleration, speed, etc. of the books, his understanding on the situation let's his Will work and the books go to the shelf. Is that it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-31T17:40:40-07:00","id":1328650,"title":"","content":"If your Mage believes it works, probably. &quot;By knowing every factor I can make it so with my will&quot;<br /> Sounds like a fun enough concept. Would take some time and some science know how (or you could substitute physics knowledge with alchemy and stuff)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25315-jihelu","name":"Jihelu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-01T09:52:08-07:00","id":1328749,"title":"","content":"That is very much in keeping with some of the more mystical takes on the VA mindset. Though I personally would put that as more of a \u201chigh Arete\u201d situation, where computations are one of the few Instruments the Adept hasn't surpassed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-01T11:13:40-07:00","id":1328757,"title":"","content":"I imagine the addition of Computer would help, or some other instrument.<br /> <br /> Maybe even pen/paper if they find themselves without their tools.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25315-jihelu","name":"Jihelu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-01T21:57:15-07:00","id":1328878,"title":"","content":"Specifically, the Revised VA Tradition Book speaks of computations being the most important thing, and things like computers merely being aids to help with the computations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}